+# Specialty-Filtered Veterinarian Lookups Stay Out of the Vet Cache
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`VetRepository`'s two unfiltered reads are annotated `@Cacheable("vets")`. `CacheConfiguration` creates that cache through the JCache API and sets no size limit. Its own javadoc records that a size limit must come from the selected provider's configuration mechanism. No such provider configuration is committed. No eviction is configured either — that gap is [Open Question 5](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey).
+
+`REQ-VET-003` adds a lookup that takes a specialty name supplied by the caller. Two keys today come from the code: the empty key of `findAll()` and the page request. A specialty name is the first cache key that a caller would choose.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Annotate the filtered lookups `@Cacheable("vets")` for consistency with their neighbours.** Rejected: the key would carry caller-supplied text into a cache with no size limit and no eviction, so any client could grow it without bound.
+2. **Filter the cached full list inside the controller.** Rejected: page numbering and totals for the narrowed set would then be computed in the web layer. That moves a data-access concern out of the repository and duplicates what Spring Data derives.
+3. **Query the database on every filtered request and leave those methods uncached** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The specialty-filtered lookups on `VetRepository` carry no cache annotation and reach the database on every request. The unfiltered reads keep their existing annotations unchanged.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A narrowed directory costs one query per request; the unnarrowed directory keeps its cache hit, so today's read path is untouched.
+- The cached key set stays bounded by what the code itself supplies, and no caller can enlarge it.
+- The asymmetry inside one repository interface is deliberate. Adding a cache annotation to a filtered lookup later requires bounding the cache first.
+- A narrowed listing always reads live data, so [Open Question 5](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) about stale vet data does not widen with this slice.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+- [`VetRepository`](../../src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetRepository.java) — the annotated and unannotated reads sit side by side.
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the current state this decision produces.
+- [REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the requirement the lookup serves.
